"},{"id":"evidence_retrieval","label":"Evidence retrieval"},{"id":"precision","label":"Precision@k"},{"id":"recall","label":"Recall@k"}]},{"citationId":"c18","pages":[{"id":"all_mpnet_base_v2","label":"all-mpnet-base-v2"},{"id":"baai_bge_large_en_v1_5","label":"BAAI/bge-large-en-v1.5"},{"id":"evidence_retrieval","label":"Evidence retrieval"},{"id":"f1_1","label":"F1@1"},{"id":"f1_10","label":"F1@10"}]},{"citationId":"c6","pages":[{"id":"baai_bge_large_en_v1_5","label":"BAAI/bge-large-en-v1.5"},{"id":"evidence_retrieval","label":"Evidence retrieval"},{"id":"qasper","label":"Qasper"}]},{"citationId":"c12","pages":[{"id":"document_retrieval","label":"document retrieval"},{"id":"evidence_retrieval","label":"Evidence retrieval"}]}],"mentions":[{"citationId":"c19"},{"citationId":"c1"},{"citationId":"c20"},{"citationId":"c21"},{"citationId":"c14"},{"citationId":"c22"},{"citationId":"c23"},{"citationId":"c13"},{"citationId":"c24"},{"citationId":"c2"}],"mentionsLeftOut":14,"citations":[{"id":"c1","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_ac7298f01655cdf6","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":1,"quote":"This study systematically evalu- ates the effectiveness of semantic chunking us- ing three common retrieval-related tasks: docu- ment retrieval, evidence retrieval, and retrieval- based answer generation."},{"id":"c2","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_3af9b0854c8045f7","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":3,"quote":"3.2 Evidence Retrieval Here we evaluate chunkers at a finer granularity than the previous experiment by measuring their abilities to locate evidence sentences."},{"id":"c3","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_267bb9040788f52b","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":4,"quote":"4.3 Evidence Retrieval As shown in Table 2, Fixed-size Chunker per- formed best on 3 out of 5 datasets, indicating a slight edge in capturing core evidence sentences."},{"id":"c4","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_9e8e482cc4774faa","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":10,"quote":"In Figure 2, evidence retrieval shows an inverse trend. As chunk size decreases, fewer sentences are retrieved, lowering the chance of retrieving ev- idence sentences and causing a sharp decline in recall."},{"id":"c5","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_fc69e0b6eebd261b","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":3,"quote":"The results for Answer Generation closely matched those of Evidence Retrieval and are discussed in Appendix E.1."},{"id":"c6","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_c2e40781dd6e6a5d","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":13,"quote":"3.89 10.73 10.72 9.24 6.39 Qasper 7.80 6.20 5.34 6.88 6.83 6.76 6.59 6.43 5.70 4.99 4.71 4.34 Table 10: F1 scores for all k values for Evidence Retrieval (%), from BAAI/bge-large-en-v1.5."},{"id":"c7","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_db87287a4bc97586","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":14,"quote":"hyperparameter values for Breakpoint-based Semantic Chunker. Left: Document Retrieval; Right: Evidence Retrieval."},{"id":"c8","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_db87287a4bc97586","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":14,"quote":"hyperparameter values for Clustering-based Semantic Chunker (DBSCAN). Left: Document Retrieval; Right: Evidence Retrieval."},{"id":"c9","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_10f57c2260ce3d16","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":9,"quote":"See Table 9 for F1 scores at all k values for evidence retrieval."},{"id":"c10","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_ac39d168a20f05cd","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":9,"quote":"Evidence Retrieval In evidence retrieval, recall and precision are sensitive to chunk size when con- sidered separately."},{"id":"c11","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_b75e903e43c22aaf","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":10,"quote":"See Tables 9-11 for full F1 scores from the three embedding models on evidence retrieval."},{"id":"c12","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_c3934d34d638707b","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":8,"quote":"This creates a coarser granularity for document retrieval and motivated the need for the evidence retrieval experiment, which offers a finer level of evaluation."},{"id":"c13","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_523725d1f0094d60","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":2,"quote":"3 Experiments In the absence of ground-truth chunk data, we de- signed three experiments to indirectly assess the quality of each chunker: document retrieval, evi- dence retrieval, and answer generation."},{"id":"c14","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_62e78ed097a9e5e1","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":1,"quote":"Therefore, we design an indirect evaluation using three proxy tasks: (1) doc- ument retrieval, measuring the ability to identify relevant documents; (2) evidence retrieval, mea- suring the ability to locate ground-truth evidence; and (3)"},{"id":"c15","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_7b79964ed96d7d7b","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":4,"quote":"5 Conclusion In this paper, we evaluated semantic and fixed-size chunking strategies in RAG systems across docu- ment retrieval, evidence retrieval, and answer gen- eration."},{"id":"c16","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_8eb1cce3ff0dd0c1","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":10,"quote":"As seen in Figure 3, this leads to a decrease in precision and an increase in recall for document and evidence retrieval, respectively, similar to the single-linkage case."},{"id":"c17","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_8eb1cce3ff0dd0c1","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":10,"quote":"In Figure 4, we observe similar trends to Figure 2 and 3: as chunk size increases, precision decreases in both retrieval tasks, while recall increases sharply for evidence retrieval."},{"id":"c18","chunkId":"8bbe93a93b05967d_c_b75e903e43c22aaf","docId":"8bbe93a93b05967d","docTitle":"2410.13070_Is_Semantic_Chunking_Worth_the_Computational_Cost","page":10,"quote":"In the Evidence Retrieval exper- iment, BAAI/bge-large-en-v1.5 outperformed all-mpnet-base-v2 by 1.06% on F1@1 and 1.32% on F1@10, both statistically significant at the 5% level."},{"id":"c19","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_154fdb662f9e1554","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":17,"quote":"Surdeanu, “Divide & conquer for entailment-aware multi-hop evidence retrieval,” arXiv preprint arXiv:2311.02616, 2023."},{"id":"c20","chunkId":"d2068edc08df316d_c_b13304b864842c88","docId":"d2068edc08df316d","docTitle":"Siren's Song in the AI Ocean: A Survey on Hallucination in Large Language Models","page":17,"quote":"The evidence retrieval process typically employs various sparse (e.g., BM25 (Robertson et al., 2009)) or dense (e.g., PLM-based meth- ods (Zhao et al., 2022)) retrievers."},{"id":"c21","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_8a48f89241609c2a","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":17,"quote":"